    "description": "Naked Pea has one ingredient, yellow pea protein, which the brand says is sourced from the United States and Canada. Per the label it delivers about 27 g of protein in roughly 120 calories with no sweetener, gums or flavorings. That makes it the cheapest and simplest way to get a dairy-free protein, and the easiest to blend into smoothies or baking.",
    "pros": [
      "One ingredient, with no sweeteners, gums or flavorings",
      "About 27 g of protein in roughly 120 calories",
      "Budget-tier cost per 25 g of protein"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Earthy taste and gritty texture in water, as buyers commonly report",
      "No NSF or Informed Choice certification we could confirm",
      "Pea is a legume, so it may not suit people with a legume or peanut allergy"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The cleanest, cheapest dairy-free base if you blend your shakes.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "About 27 g (label)",
      "Calories": "About 120",
      "Third-party tested": "No sport certification confirmed",
      "Best for": "Vegans, budget, smoothies"
